---
import Container from "@moesegfault/style/astro/Container.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
const root = "https://style.moesegfault.dev";
---
<DocsLayout title="Distribution" description="Versioned static asset paths and update policy for MoeSegFault Style." currentPath="/en/distribution/" locale="en">
  <header class="page-intro"><Container><p class="kicker">DISTRIBUTION</p><h1>Pick a URL and start using it.</h1><p class="lede">No npm installation is required. Copy a pinned URL for predictable updates, or choose latest to follow each new stable release automatically.</p></Container></header>
  <section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="paths-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Asset map</p><h2 id="paths-title">Ready-to-use resources</h2></div></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Pinned URL</th><th>When to use it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Complete styles</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/all.css</code></td><td>The easiest option: load the complete visual system</td></tr><tr><td>Design tokens</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/tokens.css</code></td><td>Use only the color, spacing, radius, and other CSS variables</td></tr><tr><td>Foundations</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/foundation.css</code></td><td>Add themes and base typography without component appearance</td></tr><tr><td>Components</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/components.css</code></td><td>Add component appearance after loading the foundations</td></tr><tr><td>Token JSON</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/tokens/tokens.json</code></td><td>Read resolved tokens from an application or build script</td></tr><tr><td>DTCG JSON</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/tokens/tokens.dtcg.json</code></td><td>Import tokens into a DTCG-compatible design or conversion tool</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div></Container></section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="strategy-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Choose a path</p><h2 id="strategy-title">How should your copy update?</h2></div></div><div class="asset-grid">
    <article class="asset-card"><h3>Recommended: pin a version</h3><p>Content under <code>/v0.1.1/…</code> never changes, so a new library release cannot unexpectedly alter your page. When you are ready to upgrade, replace the version number in the URL.</p><CodeBlock label="HTML" code={`<link rel="stylesheet"\n  href="${root}/v0.1.1/css/all.css">`} /></article>
    <article class="asset-card"><h3>Use only the latest foundations</h3><p><code>/css</code>, <code>/tokens</code>, and <code>/colors</code> follow the newest stable release automatically. Browse colors at <code>/colors</code>, or use the CSS and JSON files directly.</p><CodeBlock label="HTML" code={`<link rel="stylesheet"\n  href="${root}/css/all.css">`} /></article>
    <article class="asset-card"><h3>Use the latest complete version</h3><p><code>/latest/…</code> always follows the newest stable release. It works well for examples, personal pages, and projects that welcome automatic updates; pin a version for important applications.</p><CodeBlock label="HTML" code={`<link rel="stylesheet"\n  href="${root}/latest/css/all.css">`} /></article>
  </div><div class="callout"><h3>Not sure which one to choose?</h3><p>Use <code>/v0.1.1/…</code> for a production project and <code>/latest/…</code> for a prototype or showcase. Browser and edge caches may make latest updates appear a little later, but pinned URLs are unaffected.</p></div></Container></section>
  <section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="release-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Versions</p><h2 id="release-title">Find versions and upgrade</h2></div></div><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-number">01</span><h3>See every version</h3><p>Open the root <code>/manifest.json</code> to find every available version and its manifest URL.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-number">02</span><h3>Upgrade when you choose</h3><p>After confirming that a new version fits your needs, replace the version number in your asset URL.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-number">03</span><h3>Keep using older versions</h3><p>Every exact version remains available independently, so pages that are not ready to upgrade can keep their existing URL.</p></article></div></Container></section>
</DocsLayout>
